1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,500
Tepera "Scrolling hours" beta
AccessibilityService demo

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,800
Settings: "Idea over the feed"
needs the Accessibility permission

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:20,800
Prominent disclosure: what the service sees, why,
and that Tepera sends nothing anywhere

4
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:26,300
User declines ("Not now").
Accessibility stays off

5
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:32,800
The disclosure can be opened again

6
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:44,800
User agrees ("I agree") and is sent to
Android's own Accessibility settings

7
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:55,300
The service description in Android settings
explains exactly what it does

8
00:00:55,800 --> 00:01:02,800
User turns it on and confirms
in the system dialog

9
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:15,300
Access granted by the user: the service is on

10
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,500
Back in Tepera

11
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:34,500
The user decides if "Idea over the feed" is on
and which apps count as feeds

12
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Feed apps: chosen by the user
(here: Calculator)

13
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:45,000
Scrolling hour set by the user: 10:00-13:00

14
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:53,500
Opening a chosen feed inside that hour:
Tepera shows its own suggestion over the app

15
00:01:53,900 --> 00:02:03,000
The user can always continue:
"Open for 5 min" opens the app

16
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:07,700
Five minutes later, the app is still open

17
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:18,700
After the timer the user chose: a dimming layer
with "5 more" / "Leave" buttons

18
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:23,200
The user taps "Leave" and returns
to the home screen

19
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:30,200
Other apps are not affected:
no suggestion appears

20
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:41,200
The user can turn the service off
at any time in Android settings

21
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:47,700
The service is turned off

22
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:50,500
End of demo

